{
  "case_id": "2008-07-581",
  "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Paul Salvatore",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are three reasons why this Court should reverse the Second Circuit's blanket ban on collectively bargained, arbitral forum -- forum selection clauses. First, the Second Circuit ignored section (a) of the National Labor Relations Act, by which Congress empowered unions to bargain on behalf of their employees over anything germane to the working environment, including methods of workplace dispute resolution. The forum in which an ADEA claim is heard falls squarely in that authority. Indeed, forbidding unions from bargaining about the procedural right to an arbitral forum will carve a judicial exception into the labor law permitting employers to bypass the union and deal directly with their employees, defeating Congress's"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul Salvatore",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, the Second Circuit failed to consider Congress's strong endorsement of workplace arbitration contained in both the FAA and section 301. Third, the Second Circuit erroneously and exclusively relied on Alexander versus Gardner-Denver. Gardner-Denver is a case about claim preclusion, not about enforcing an agreement to arbitrate a statutory claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Salvatore, you take the position that the only thing that is at stake here is simply, in effect, a selection of the arbitral forum. What do you -- what do you say to the argument that, in fact, the -- under -- under the collective bargaining agreement the employee is subject not merely to the right of the union to choose the arbitral forum, but, in fact, to -- to assert any claim at all? What -- what is your answer to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where does -- where does the contract say anything about the -- the individual succeeding to whatever arrangement there is between the union and the employer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul Salvatore",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Second Circuit did not consider it. Indeed, the Second Circuit found that the clause covered these employees, and -- and this only came up in the Respondents' brief in this Court after cert was granted, the red brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WHERE DID WE GET THIS PHRASE -- WHERE DO WE GET THE LANGUAGE \"OR THE UNION WILL TURN OVER TO THEM\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WHERE -- WHERE IS THE GUARANTEE THAT THE -- IF THE UNION SAYS, WE DON'T WANT TO TOUCH THIS, AS IN THIS CASE, THAT THE EMPLOYEE HAS THE RIGHT EITHER TO ARBITRATE OR, FOR THAT MATTER, TO SUE? WHERE DO YOU FIND THAT?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul Salvatore",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's the practice under this agreement, Your Honor. We would -- we would wholeheartedly endorse that -- that rule because, that's the practice here. And there is -- when you're talking about statutory rights, why would the union want to interfere with the ability of the employee to get a forum if their interests are not aligned? This goes to the tension that this Court has -- has recognized in its prior cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SALVATORE, WOULD YOU -- WOULD YOU OBJECT TO OR OPPOSE A RULING THAT SAID -- THAT SAYS YES, THE -- THE RIGHT CAN BE SUBJECTED TO UNION ARBITRATION, BUT IF THE UNION CHOOSES NOT TO ARBITRATE IT THE INDIVIDUAL MUST HAVE THE RIGHT TO ARBITRATE IT ON HIS OWN?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: You said -- the -- fine. I -- I grasp your answer to that. But you said that the employee would have the absolute right if the union says, \"sorry, for whatever reason we can't represent you,\" absolute right to that arbitral forum. What -- who pays then?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. SALVATORE",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SALVATORE: In -- in this situation the employer pays. That's the only -- the Office of the Contract Arbitrator is an -- essentially a mini- American Arbitration Association that these parties have set up, and the -- the RAB, which is the multi- employer organization that represents all the real estate employers in -- in New York, they pay for the arbitration, because the union in this case has said we are not going to pay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREDERICK: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Second Circuit's judgment should be affirmed for three reasons. First, a collective bargaining agreement gives the union exclusive control over workers' grievances. Second, unions have inherent conflicts of interest with respect to individual statutory anti-discrimination rights; and third, unions lack authority to serve as gatekeepers of individual workers' substantive ADEA rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Under your first point, are you saying it's impossible for there to be a collective bargaining agreement that reads the way Mr. Salvatore reads this collective bargaining agreement; a collective bargaining agreement which says that the union's -- that the grievance must be arbitrated, and it will be done either by the union, or if the union declines to pursue it, by the individual employee?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to cert we specifically raise the issue that the union controls the arbitration, and there is no opportunity for individual arbitration under this collective bargaining agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You did raise that issue, but you didn't say that the consequence of that issue was that you win."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about the argument that you are -- if you win this case, you are subjecting the employee to a worse situation because the employer will simply say: Fine, I don't have to bargain anything with the union."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF CURTIS E. GANNON"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents' fundamental right to a workplace free of invidious, class-based discrimination is something their union has no power to barter away in collective bargaining, and the union --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0002-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, we don't think that there is any reason why the employees will not be able to make a grievance with the employers, as was made possible in Gilmer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0002-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that there needs to be individual agreement in order to comply with Gilmer because of the underlying inherent tension between the collective interest of the union and the individual interests of the employees, especially in anti-discrimination statutes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: I mean, they didn't turn it over, did they, until the action had been brought in the Federal court? I mean, they didn't -- maybe I'm wrong in this, but I didn't think that on day one they -- they said, oh, well, because the union doesn't want to proceed with this, you're welcome to chug ahead by yourself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Union",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SALVATORE: Yes, Justice Ginsburg. And there are -- are several points. First, there is no conflict here in this case. The union did the right thing. It turned the claim over to the individual employees with their private counsel and let them go arbitrate it themselves. They refused. This isn't a Magnavox situation. The union is not --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What happened here was the claim was originally tendered by these employees to the union to bring an arbitration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f775f4efe490-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At that point the record is clear that demand was made on -- on the employee's counsel, Mr. Kreisberg -- it's in his affidavit -- that -- that he returned to Arbitrator Pfeiffer to the pending arbitration and continue in that forum, and he refused to. That was the basis of the motion to compel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-581",
      "confidence": 0.0,
